      "status": "ok",
      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence supports that the authors address why Twitter predicts language inventory better: the Discussion reports that Twitter has fewer missing languages (fewer false negatives) than web-crawled data, and the Population Demographics section attributes part of the better representation to the prevalence of common languages like English and Spanish on Twitter plus better representation of North America and Oceania. The authors also discuss platform biases (wealthier/urban populations) but do not single out one causal hypothesis; the closest explicit explanation combines fewer missing languages and language-commonness effects."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 2827.147600000899
    },
    {
      "stage": "Generate",
